{"id":"n-20261008-ovi68g","category":"tech","display_title":"Xbox Launches XP Entertainment Division","display_title_he":"אקס‌בוקס משיקה את חטיבת הבידור XP","short_summary":"Microsoft has established a new entertainment division named XP to expand its major gaming franchises into film, television, live events, and consumer products.","english_level":"C1","words":512,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/XBox_One_Launch_E3-1681.jpg/960px-XBox_One_Launch_E3-1681.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Microsoft · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XBox_One_Launch_E3-1681.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/xbox-announces-new-xp-entertainment-division-to-make-movies-tv-and-more","title":"Xbox Announces New XP Entertainment Division to Make Movies, TV, and More","published_at":"2026-10-08T12:00:22.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T12:00:22.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-08T15:22:19.954Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Microsoft has officially announced the creation of a brand new entertainment division called XP, designed to expand its major video game franchises far beyond the boundaries of the console itself. The overarching ambition behind this move is to position Xbox as the foremost gaming and entertainment enterprise globally. According to company announcements, the division will be led by Kayleen Walters, a Lucasfilm veteran who previously served as president of Mojang and acted as an executive producer on last year's cinematic adaptation of Minecraft.","Rather than operating as a traditional in-house production studio, XP aims to collaborate with external partners across four core investment areas: Xbox Pictures, Xbox Products, Xbox Partnerships, and Xbox Places. The title itself is a clever play on Experience Points. These distinct pillars will oversee film and television adaptations, consumer merchandise and licensing, brand sponsorships, and physical location-based experiences such as upcoming theme parks, major brand takeovers, and marquee live broadcasts.","Company leadership emphasized that successful media adaptations have historically driven massive engagement back to the core games themselves. For instance, Amazon's Fallout television series helped trigger a significant fivefold surge in hours played on Game Pass during its debut season, while weekly active users for Minecraft jumped by over seventy-five percent year-over-year following the release of its movie. Upcoming adaptations already confirmed in the pipeline include a movie sequel titled Minecraft Squared, the third season of Fallout, a collaborative Call of Duty film project helmed by Peter Berg and Taylor Sheridan, and an animated Diablo series with Netflix. Furthermore, the spiritual successor Physint by Hideo Kojima includes film and television rights, pointing toward future adaptations.","Live events also play a monumental role in this strategy. Blizzard's BlizzCon recently drew thirty-five thousand physical attendees in Anaheim alongside twelve and a half million digital viewers at home, while Minecraft Live reached more than one hundred forty-four million people. Physical ventures are expanding as well, with a dedicated Minecraft theme park scheduled to open its gates next year, alongside varied consumer collaborations such as an Ikea furniture range and a Gears of War takeover with WWE.","This strategic restructuring recalls past attempts by Microsoft to conquer the entertainment space, most notably the short-lived Xbox Entertainment Studios launched back in the Xbox 360 era. That previous initiative sought to produce exclusive shows for consoles — including an original Halo project announced by Steven Spielberg — but shuttered after just two years following the troubled launch of the Xbox One in 2013. Today, executives believe the current market landscape offers much stronger opportunities for cross-media synergy amid an ongoing corporate reset.","Alongside the launch of XP, significant leadership changes were also announced at Mojang. Maria Angelidou-Smith, who previously held high-profile product and engineering roles at Meta, Personio, and Reddit where she served as Chief Product Officer, is stepping in as the new CEO of Mojang. She brings extensive experience in building products used by billions of people to guide the studio through its next phase of growth, taking over as Minecraft remains the best-selling video game of all time with over four hundred twenty-five million copies shifted."],"facts":[{"fact":"Xbox announced a new entertainment division called XP to handle movies, TV, products, partnerships, and places.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The division is headed by Lucasfilm veteran Kayleen Walters, former president of Mojang.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Maria Angelidou-Smith joins Xbox as the new CEO of Mojang.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Microsoft","lemma":"Microsoft","pos":"PROPN","he":"מייקרוסופט","name":"true"},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"ADV","he":"רשמית","name":false},{"text":"announced","lemma":"announce","pos":"VERB","he":"הכריז","name":false},{"text":"creation","lemma":"creation","pos":"NOUN","he":"הקים / יצירה","name":false},{"text":"brand new","lemma":"brand new","pos":"ADJ","he":"חדש לגמרי","name":false},{"text":"entertainment","lemma":"entertainment","pos":"NOUN","he":"בידור","name":false},{"text":"division","lemma":"division","pos":"NOUN","he":"חטיבה","name":false},{"text":"XP","lemma":"XP","pos":"PROPN","he":"אקס-פי","name":"true"},{"text":"designed","lemma":"design","pos":"VERB","he":"מותאם / מעוצב","name":false},{"text":"expand","lemma":"expand","pos":"VERB","he":"להרחיב","name":false},{"text":"major","lemma":"major","pos":"ADJ","he":"מרכזי / ראשי","name":false},{"text":"video game",